an10.12:4.3 starts: restlessness, and doubt are
an10.12:4.4 starts: totally absent in a bhikkhu;
an10.12:5.1 starts: when one like this possesses
an10.12:5.2 starts: the virtue and concentration
an10.12:5.3 starts: of one beyond training,
an10.12:5.4 starts: and similar liberation and knowledge;
an3.30:4.3 starts: often goes to visit bhikkhus
an3.30:4.4 starts: to hear them teach the Dhamma.
an3.30:6.3 starts: He too often goes to visit bhikkhus
an3.30:6.4 starts: to hear them teach the Dhamma.
# superseded: an3.30:7.2 starts: While sitting in his seat,
an3.30:7.3 starts: he grasps the phrasing of the talk,
an3.30:7.4 starts: at its beginning, middle, and end.
an3.30:8.3 starts: He too often goes to visit bhikkhus
an3.30:8.4 starts: to hear them teach the Dhamma.
an3.34:13.1 starts: Whatever kamma an ignorant person has done
an3.34:13.2 starts: born of greed, hatred, and delusion,
an3.34:13.3 starts: whether what was fashioned by him be
an3.34:13.4 none
an3.39:8.2 starts: old age, and death, are disgusted
an3.39:8.3 starts: by other people who exist
an3.39:8.4 starts: in accordance with their nature.
an3.39:10.4 starts: intoxication with health,
# superseded: an3.39:11.1 none
